 ### Two-Pass Image Transformation
-The original method by Drebin et al. transforms the volume in two stages [S1, unofficial]. It is less efficient and produces lower quality for general views compared to the three-pass method [S1, unofficial].
+The original method by Drebin et al. transforms the volume in two stages. It is less efficient and produces lower quality for general views compared to the three-pass method. Choose this variant for simpler implementations where general view quality is not critical. [Two-Pass Image Transformation](4114-two-pass-image-transformation.md)
 
 ### Three-Pass Image Transformation
-Generalized by Hanrahan. It decomposes the transformation into three passes to reduce resampling stages and improve efficiency and quality for general views [S1, unofficial].
+Generalized by Hanrahan, this method decomposes the transformation into three passes to reduce resampling stages and improve efficiency and quality for general views. Choose this variant when higher rendering quality and time efficiency for arbitrary viewpoints are required. [Three-Pass Image Transformation](4116-three-pass-image-transformation.md)
 
